---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RevealH1 from '../../components/RevealH1.astro';
import ClosingCTA from '../../components/ClosingCTA.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Edoardo Rossi — marketing as the meeting point between business and psychology: understanding people through data, and data through people."
  translated
>
  <section class="about container">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <RevealH1 text="Marketing is where business meets psychology." />
    <p class="lede">
      That's what brought me here, and it's what keeps me here. Behind every metric is a
      behavior. Behind every behavior, a person making a decision. The anthropological side of
      the job — understanding who you're talking to, what they're really after, why they choose
      — interests me just as much as the analytical one. If anything, I don't think one works
      without the other.
    </p>
    <p>
      Data on its own tells you what happened. People on their own tell stories the numbers
      sometimes contradict. My work sits in between — using analysis to answer who, what and why,
      then using those answers to build campaigns, funnels and positioning that treat an audience
      as people, not segments.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm always looking for the extra step: the process behind the campaign, the business behind
      the brief, the outcome behind the report. My <a href={`${base}en/work/`}>case studies</a>
      show how that plays out in practice — real numbers, stated limitations included.
    </p>
  </section>

  <ClosingCTA />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about { padding-block: var(--space-6); max-width: 46rem; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; }
</style>
